    <briefdescription>
<para>Represents the root node of the spatial tree in the landscape. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="class_root_terrain_cell" kindref="compound">RootTerrainCell</ref> is the top-level branch of the spatial tree. It inherits from <ref refid="class_branch_terrain_cell" kindref="compound">BranchTerrainCell</ref> and represents the starting point for all recursive operations on the spatial tree, including:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="class_animal" kindref="compound">Animal</ref> insertion, migration, and evaluation.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Resource and moisture deserialization and updates.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Applying functions to animals and resources recursively.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Unlike other branches, the root cell has no parent, so <ref refid="class_root_terrain_cell_1af0daefd5391a201570cbbae08f738b4d" kindref="member">getParent()</ref> returns nullptr. It overrides certain methods to handle operations starting from the top of the tree. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
